<title>USA: Harmon Indus has large GE contract.</title>
<headline>Harmon Indus has large GE contract.</headline>
<dateline>BLUE SPRINGS, Mo. 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harmon Industries Inc said Thursday it won a major new cab-signaling contract with General Electric Transportation Systems, a unit of General Electric Co.</p>
<p>The value was not disclosed.</p>
<p>Harmon, a supplier of signal and train control equipment for railroad and rail transit systems, will provide GE with 150 multi-territory Ultra Cab II units for installation in the latest model of that company's AC traction locomotives.</p>
<p>Delivery will be completed during 1997.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
